-- title:
--   The ideal content homomorphism on finite idèles
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Dedekind domain with field of fractions $K$ (so $K$ is a field, an $R$-algebra, and a fraction field of $R$). The assertion is that there exists a monoid homomorphism $\varphi$ from the unit group of the finite adèle ring `FiniteAdeleRing R K` to the unit group of the monoid of fractional ideals `FractionalIdeal R⁰ K` with the following five properties. First, $\varphi$ is pinned by an explicit factorisation: for every unit $x$, the fractional ideal underlying $\varphi(x)$ is the finitary product, over the height-one primes $v$ of $R$, of the fractional ideals $v.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ raised to the integer power $-\mathrm{log}$ of the valuation at $v$ of the $v$-th component of $x$. Second, for $k \in K^{\times}$, $\varphi$ applied to the image of $k$ under the unit-group map induced by $K \to$ `FiniteAdeleRing R K` is the principal fractional ideal $(k)$, i.e. `toPrincipalIdeal R K k`. Third, $\varphi$ is surjective. Fourth, the kernel of $\varphi$ is `unitIdeles R K`, the subgroup of those units $\delta$ such that for every $v$ both the $v$-th component of $\delta$ and the $v$-th component of $\delta^{-1}$ lie in the valuation ring of the completion at $v$. Fifth, for every set $T$ of height-one primes of $R$ and every unit $x$: $x$ lies in the join of the image of $K^{\times}$ and of `unitIdelesOutside R K T`, the subgroup of units $\delta$ whose components $\delta_v$ and $(\delta^{-1})_v$ are integral at every $v \notin T$, if and only if the ideal class `ClassGroup.mk K (φ x)` lies in the subgroup of `ClassGroup R` generated by the classes `ClassGroup.mk0 ⟨v.asIdeal, h⟩` for $v \in T$ (with $h$ a witness that $v.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ is a non-zero-divisor in `Ideal R`).
--
--   This is the idèlic description of the ideal class group in value-pinned form: the content map sends a finite idèle to the fractional ideal $\prod_v \mathfrak{p}_v^{\mathrm{ord}_v(x_v)}$, restricts to the principal-ideal map on $K^{\times}$, and has the unit idèles as kernel; the last clause refines the resulting isomorphism to the $T$-class group, identifying $\mathbb{A}_K^{f,\times}/K^{\times}U^{T}$ with $\mathrm{Cl}(R)$ modulo the classes of the primes in $T$. It is used in the treatment of idèlic class-group quotients and local inverse maps, for instance in establishing finite index of the product of principal and $T$-unit idèles and in estimates for class sums of automorphic forms.
-- source:
